{"content":[{"c":["BEN-AMMI"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Son born to Lot and his younger daughter. A similar incestuous liaison between Lot and his older daughter produced a son named Moab. The two sons are identified as the ancestral heads of the Ammonite and Moabite peoples (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.19.38","r":"Gen.19.38","rawR":"Gen.19.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.19.38","value":"Gen.19.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 19:38"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Although the promise made to Abraham could have been enjoyed by Lot (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.11.31","r":"Gen.11.31","rawR":"Gen.11.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.11.31","value":"Gen.11.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 11:31"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.12.1-4","r":"Gen.12.1-4","rawR":"Gen.12.1-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.12.1-4","value":"Gen.12.1-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:1-4"},"), Lot went his own way (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.13.2-12","r":"Gen.13.2-12","rawR":"Gen.13.2-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.13.2-12","value":"Gen.13.2-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:2-12"},") and failed to trust the Lord (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.19.15-23","r":"Gen.19.15-23","rawR":"Gen.19.15-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.19.15-23","value":"Gen.19.15-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:15-23"},"). Lot’s relationship to Abraham, however, evoked deferential treatment by the Israelites (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.2.8-19","r":"Deut.2.8-19","rawR":"Deut.2.8-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.2.8-19","value":"Deut.2.8-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 2:8-19"},") toward these occasionally powerful enemies (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.20.1-12","r":"2Chr.20.1-12","rawR":"2Chr.20.1-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.20.1-12","value":"2Chr.20.1-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 20:1-12"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=AmmonAmmonites_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"AmmonAmmonites_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"AmmonAmmonites_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Ammon, Ammonites"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":